+- `gpu` is the average elapsed GPU timestamp between the first and last
+  timed passes, in ms. `gpu=unavailable` means no valid timestamp was
+  collected; it does not mean zero GPU work. `gpu_parts=unavailable` means
+  per-element timestamps are unsupported or not yet available, so `g_*`
+  fields are omitted. GPU timestamps and surface acquisition waits measure
+  different things; neither alone identifies a presentation bottleneck.
+  `gpu_sample` identifies the latest valid GPU readback; repeated identifiers
+  mean repeated observations of one sample. Samples older than two seconds are
+  unavailable, not new measurements.
+  With `AURORA_PROFILE_SCENE_A=1` as well, on adapters lacking per-draw
+  timestamps, `gpu_scene_a` reports the opaque scene pass interval. These
+  extra timestamps may affect performance; compare with the option off.
